+# Transfer-design supplement — prepared, not executed
+This is an authoring guide, not a released unseen assessment item.
+Competence: identify authority, preserve history, explain behavior, derive independent negative checks and trace change impact.
+
+A structural variant may combine a future-effective jurisdiction exception with an adapter omitting policy provenance.
+A defensible response must preserve historical decisions, identify unresolved effective-scope questions, trace the consumer/test dependency and reject a silent rewrite of stored outcomes.
+Do not award credit for pattern names, memorized euro amounts or fluency without source-grounded reasoning.
+
+Before using participants:
+- Author a distinct withheld Form B; participants who saw the printed example must not be assessed with that exact example.
+- Review item difficulty and rubric anchors independently.
+- Preserve the existing two AI-assisted arms, baseline Form A and Day-14 ±2 delayed Form B.
+- Keep raw independent ratings before adjudication; report missing follow-up and critical unsafe assumptions.
+No new arms, participants, measured scores, or validated rubric are created by this supplement.
